config SIDE48_INPUT_PROCESSOR_SPIKE_FILTER
    bool "Drop physically impossible pointer deltas"
    default y
    depends on DT_HAS_SIDE48_INPUT_PROCESSOR_SPIKE_FILTER_ENABLED
    help
      The PMW3610 can return garbage motion right after waking from its
      rest modes: a burst of values near the 12 bit range with randomly
      alternating signs, which throws the cursor across the screen. Zero
      out events above the configured threshold, plus everything within a
      short window after one, so the rest of the burst is swallowed too.
      Ported from LiTom.
